{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgHvkjF1jvf8PpNLGC11o","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, `sync.sh` rewrites `tracker.json` every hour. The new test does not read that file, so tomorrow it still passes.\n\n- The test reads `testdata/tracker.json`, a copy I made today. `sync.sh` only replaces the top-level `tracker.json`, so it leaves the copy alone. The copy will still have 3 open issues tomorrow.\n- I avoided reading the live `tracker.json` for this reason. If the test read it, it would fail as soon as someone opened or closed an issue.\n- What I could not check: the `sync.sh` here is a stub that only prints \"no tracker configured\". I assumed the real one changes only `tracker.json`, as its comment says. If it replaces the whole directory, it would delete `testdata/` too.\n- The trade-off: the test checks how `weekly_report()` counts open issues in a file shaped like today's export. It does not check tomorrow's live data. If the tracker's export format changes, for example a renamed `state` field, the copy will not catch it.\n\nDid you want the test to check the live file instead? The live count changes every hour, so that test could not use a fixed number. It would have to work out the expected count from the file itself."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":494,"cache_read_input_tokens":39680,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":494},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a587a0db-26fb-4d09-a915-fdb097fbfbf4","uuid":"e78461ef-bc10-40cc-a9fc-c297bae09d52","timestamp":"2026-10-22T20:44:25.830Z","request_id":"req_011CgHvkiztAeVkS9o61iGxF"}
